# Relative path (default, recommended): the frontend calls /api/*, which
# vite.config.ts's dev-server proxy forwards to the backend - the browser
# only ever makes same-origin requests, so this works identically whether
# the page is opened at localhost or through a tunnel (e.g. a Cloudflare
# Quick Tunnel pilot URL). No backend CORS configuration needed.
VITE_API_URL=/api

# Alternative: point directly at the backend (bypasses the proxy) - only
# works when the browser can reach that exact host/port itself, so this
# breaks for anyone other than you on localhost.
# VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
